***
***	<comment from="gemini-3-flash-preview">
***	The implementation is simplified by replacing the conditional equation (ceq) with an unconditional equation using an 'if-then-else' expression. This improves efficiency in Maude because unconditional equations are generally faster to process; the 'if' construct allows the result to be determined in a single comparison regardless of which commutative permutation the engine provides, avoiding the potential overhead and backtracking logic involved in evaluating conditions in conditional rules.
***	</comment>
***

fmod MINIMUM is
	protecting NAT .

	op minimum : Nat Nat -> Nat [comm] .

	vars M N : Nat .

	eq minimum(M, N) = if M <= N then M else N fi .
endfm